<title>INDIA: India's ICI 1st half 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India's ICI 1st half 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end-September</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		179.1 vs   155.1</p>
<p>    Net sales	     3,064.1 vs 2,818.1</p>
<p>    Other income	    165.8 vs   122.5</p>
<p>    Total expenditure   2,762.6 vs 2,617.5</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   50.3 vs    17.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    103.4 vs    93.8</p>
<p>    Tax			 155.0 vs   130.0</p>
<p>NOTE: ICI India Ltd said in a statement that at a recent meeting, the board approved capital investment of more than 1.0 billion rupees covering a new paints plant at Mohali near Chandigarh, a polyurethanes systems house and R&amp;T centre for textile surfactants at Bombay, and new manufacturing capacities for packaged and bulk explosives.</p>
<p>The new paints plant in Bombay, doubling present capacity, will start operation next month.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
